Basic infrastructure-mode VHT network using Ieee80211 interfaces.

VHT sounding, packet-level beamforming, and DL MU-MIMO are disabled by
default. Their supported subset and other HT/VHT fidelity limits are described
under "HT and VHT feature scope" in the IEEE 802.11 chapter of the INET User's
Guide.

The optional VHT MU model is deliberately constrained to an AP, exactly two
associated 20 MHz users, one spatial stream per user, deterministic Group ID 1
assignment, and serialized BAR/BA exchanges. It does not model waveform
precoding or general multi-user configurations. This example is a basic VHT
network and does not configure the traffic and sounding choreography needed to
demonstrate that opt-in MU subset.
